{
 "description": "One job-local quiz mutation through a discriminated action union: form_create, form_update_draft (receipt-idempotent, expectedRevision optimistic lock), form_publish (immutable version), form_duplicate, form_archive, quiz_todo_create (server-side bind of ONE published version to a Project To-do; the server computes org id and immutable hashes; assigned quizzes are immediately worker-visible), grade (per-question awarded points + attempt-tied note), release / bulk_release (released grades become visible to that worker only), require_retake (single canonical RETURN mutation: worker-visible reason, REQUIRED expectedSubmittedAt stale-review guard, optional attemptId binding proof; grants exactly +1 attempt on the SAME version), require_retake_plan (NO-WRITE validation emitting ordered per-row commands with bounded content-derived keys and a deterministic planChecksum; also exposed as the focused read-scoped opentrain_plan_project_todo_quiz_retakes), and require_retake_apply (request-bound sequential apply of the EXACT planned rows; requires planChecksum + confirmLive=true and refuses live drift with 409 PLAN_STALE). Every write requires idempotencyKey; retries converge. FULL retakes only \u2014 selective coaching rides the dedicated opentrain_*_project_todo_quiz_coaching tools. Requires project_todos:write scope.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
